# Resolved PR:
Implements the student available-exam list and strict server-side window enforcement for the Online Exam Portal in accordance with FR-05, SEC-REQ-02, SEC-OBJ-01, and NFR-04.

This PR also integrates the latest changes from main and registers the core app with explicit namespacing to ensure all existing modules (accounts, exams, core) function seamlessly.

Key Changes
Student Available-Exam List (accounts/views.py, student_dashboard.html):

Queries configured exams ordered chronologically by scheduled start_at.
Renders a responsive table displaying exam title, duration, formatted scheduled window timestamps, and availability status.
Status indicators:
Available Now: Current time is within window; renders an active Start Exam button.
Upcoming: Current time is before start_at; action button is disabled.
Closed: Window has elapsed (now > end_at); action button is disabled.
Server-Side Window Enforcement (exams/views.py, take_exam.html):

Guards exam attempts at /exams/<id>/take/ and /exams/<id>/:
Early Access Guard: Rejects access before start_at with HTTP 403 Forbidden ("This exam has not started yet. Early access is blocked on server.").
Expired Access Guard: Rejects access after end_at with HTTP 403 Forbidden ("This exam availability window has expired. Access is blocked on server.").
Active Window: Grants access (HTTP 200 OK) and renders attempt rules and metadata.
Enforces @login_required redirecting unauthenticated users to /accounts/login/ (HTTP 302).
Supports REST API clients returning JSON responses (Accept: application/json or ?format=json).
Core App & Test Harness Cleanup:

Registered core app in INSTALLED_APPS and added app_name = 'core' to core/urls.py to fix reverse namespace resolution.